\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. How sweet the name of Jesus sounds
\par In a believer's ear!
\par It soothes his sorrows, heals his wounds,
\par And drives away his fear.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. It makes the wounded spirit whole,
\par And calms the troubled breast;
\par 'Tis manna to the hungry soul,
\par And to the weary rest.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Dear name! the Rock on which I build,
\par My shield, and hiding-place,
\par My never-fallen treasury, filled
\par With boundless stores of grace!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Jesus, my Shepherd, Brother, Friend,
\par My Prophet, Priest, and King,
\par My Lord, my Life, my Way, my End,
\par Accept the praise I bring.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Weak is the effort of my heart,
\par And cold my warmest thought,
\par But when I see Thee as Thou art
\par I'll praise Thee as I ought.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Till then I would Thy love proclaim
\par With every fleeting breath;
\par And may the music of Thy name
\par Refresh my soul in death.
\par                               Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

